<title>USA: Salomon hires ex-Chase banker for new unit.</title>
<headline>Salomon hires ex-Chase banker for new unit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers, investment banking unit of Salomon Inc, said it hired Nazan Clohesy, formerly of Chase Securities Inc, to direct bank loan sales in a new bank loan group.</p>
<p>At Chase Securities, a unit of Chase Manhattan Corp, Clohesy was a vice president in the global syndicated finance group focusing on sales and distribution of highly leveraged bank loans.</p>
<p>The bank loan group at Salomon Brothers reports to Richard Ivers, a managing director who recently joined the firm from CS First Boston.</p>
</text>
